# 01 iOS Architecture

## Goal
Keep architecture consistent, testable, and scalable for an iOS-first app.

## Architecture defaults
- SwiftUI-first implementation.
- Feature-based folder structure.
- MVVM (or equivalent clear separation of concerns).
- Explicit async state modeling.

## Always
- Keep business logic in ViewModel, service, or domain layers.
- Keep views declarative and UI-focused.
- Define clear boundaries for models, services, and state.
- Keep naming consistent and human-readable.
- Ensure new features can be unit tested.

## Prohibited
- Network or persistence logic inline in SwiftUI views.
- God objects with mixed responsibilities.
- Ad-hoc global state unless strictly necessary and documented.
